## Result of This Configuration

After completing these steps, the Jump Host can execute remote commands, run scripts, or orchestrate automation across all application servers without manual password entry. This configuration forms the foundation for tools such as Ansible, Jenkins agents, remote deployments, and system monitoring workflows.

With secure key-based authentication in place, the environment is ready for centralized automation tasks.
